    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8fm0-01-2022-june/q1",
      "question": "<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{A} = \\begin{pmatrix} 4 &amp; -1 \\\\ 7 &amp; 2 \\\\ -5 &amp; 8 \\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{B} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 &amp; 3 &amp; 2 \\\\ -1 &amp; 6 &amp; 5 \\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{C} = \\begin{pmatrix} -5 &amp; 2 &amp; 1 \\\\ 4 &amp; 3 &amp; 8 \\\\ -6 &amp; 11 &amp; 2 \\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{I}\"></span> is the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3 \\times 3\"></span> identity matrix,</p><p>(a) (i) show that there is an integer <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> for which</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{AB} - 3\\mathbf{C} + k\\mathbf{I} = \\mathbf{0}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>stating the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span></p><p>(ii) explain why there can be no constant <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\"></span> such that</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{BA} - 3\\mathbf{C} + m\\mathbf{I} = \\mathbf{0}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p><p>(b) (i) Show how the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{C}\"></span> can be used to solve the simultaneous equations</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"-5x + 2y + z = -14\" data-display=\"true\"></div><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"4x + 3y + 8z = 3\" data-display=\"true\"></div><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"-6x + 11y + 2z = 7\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>(ii) Hence use your calculator to solve these equations.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p>",
      "steps": [
