      "id": "exam/edexcel-8fm0-01-2022-june/q5",
      "question": "<p>(a) Use the standard summation formulae to show that, for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n \\in \\mathbb{N}\"></span>,</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{n} \\left(3r^2 - 17r - 25\\right) = n\\left(n^2 - An - B\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> are integers to be determined.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p><p>(b) Explain why, for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k \\in \\mathbb{N}\"></span>,</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=1}^{3k} r \\tan(60r)^\\circ = -k\\sqrt{3}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>Using the results from part (a) and part (b) and showing all your working,</p><p>(c) determine any value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\"></span> that satisfies</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sum_{r=5}^{n} \\left(3r^2 - 17r - 25\\right) = 15\\left[\\sum_{r=6}^{3n} r \\tan(60r)^\\circ\\right]^2\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p><span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></p>",
      "steps": [
